LightMoss: leave the G80CA's eMMC pins alone.

rk_board_late_init() muxed GPIO1_A0, A1, A4 and B1 to the SPI flash
controller (board_init_sfc_if) and GPIO1_A2, A5-A7 and B4-B7 to plain
GPIO for buttons (board_init_switch_gpio). On the boards this was
written for that is where SPI flash and buttons are; on the G80CA,
GPIO1_A0-A7 are the internal eMMC's data lines and B1 its clock. Everything after it (the boot logo, the charging pictures,
the "no SD card" check, cfgload) then failed to read the eMMC, so with
TF1 empty LightMoss on the eMMC never started: the "no SD card" screen,
then power-off. Neither is called now.

--- a/board/rockchip/odroidgoa/odroidgoa.c
+++ b/board/rockchip/odroidgoa/odroidgoa.c
@@ -210,11 +210,21 @@
 	/* set uart2-m1 port as a default debug console */
 	board_debug_uart2m1();
 
+	/*
+	 * LightMoss: neither on the G80CA. Its internal eMMC is on these GPIO1
+	 * pins, where the boards this code was written for have SPI flash and
+	 * buttons: muxing them to SFC and to GPIO cut U-Boot off from the eMMC
+	 * from here on, so a system on it never started with TF1 empty (the
+	 * "no SD card" screen). Linux muxes them for the eMMC itself, which is
+	 * why the eMMC worked there.
+	 */
+#if 0
 	/* set sfc alternate function */
 	board_init_sfc_if();
 
 	/* set switch gpio */
 	board_init_switch_gpio();
+#endif
 
 	/* check power */
 	if(board_check_power())
